From 2fc48d245faca37e40952a8c94f5c2078426b82c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JustFoura <JustFoura.dev@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:02:10 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] Staging gate fix + copy read-ahead (prefill wall root
 cause); land the day's env-gated decode experiments
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Evening root cause: with --cpu-moe + mmap the expert weights live in
CPU_Mapped buffers (a plain file mmap). The graph scheduler copies every
expert tensor into a device buffer BEFORE each prompt-pass mul_mat_id —
~77 GB per one-pass prefill through fully synchronous per-tensor writes
whose mmap read side sustains only ~0.9 GB/s (GPU busy 45%, CPU 0.9 cores;
ubatch sweep read volumes 77/138/259 GB at 16384/8192/4096 = copies per
pass). The device-staging gate qualified src0 via the pinned-memory lookup,
which cannot see CPU_Mapped pointers, so staging silently skipped 100% of
ops (143k major faults with the flag on) and the 09-29 'compute-bound'
verdict measured a no-op. Fix: qualify on host-backed src0 and stage from
the raw pointer; broken-flag fallback when staging buffers cannot allocate.
Also: rolling POSIX_FADV_WILLNEED copy read-ahead in
ggml_backend_vk_buffer_set_tensor (LLAMA_VK_COPY_READAHEAD_MB, default
1536, 0=off) — parity byte-identical, measured neutral so far (the window
is file-adjacent while the sched copies are graph-ordered); one-time
stage-gate instrumentation line kept for the next pass.

Also lands the day session's env-gated experiments (documented in
bench-results-2026-10-01/FINDINGS.md): LLAMA_MOE_MISS_PREFETCH (loss),
LLAMA_MOE_FANOUT_PIPE (neutral), LLAMA_MOE_PROMPT_PREREAD (neutral — its
registry only fills from CPU mul_mat_id, which never runs at prompt
widths), LLAMA_VK_MOE_DEVICE_STAGE (the no-op analyzed above).
